sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/approach/grn-memory-generic-or-biological--grok-4-7--1> a prov:Plan, delphi:TestableHypothesis ;
    rdfs:label "Match 350 random ODE networks to the 35 BioModels" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/grn-memory-generic-or-biological> ;
    dct:description "Re-run the Biswas, Manicka, Hoel and Levin 2021 memory probes on the original models they took from BioModels, and on at least 10 random networks per model, at least 350 in total. Match each random network on node count, reaction count, and kinetic family (mass-action or Hill, matching the source model). Draw parameter magnitudes from the empirical distribution of the absolute values in that source model. Randomize regulatory signs in this approach; the topology-preserving arm is the next one. Probes are the paper's UCS-based, pairing, associative and consolidation memories, plus habituation. The enrichment statistic is the paired difference in the number of memory kinds present. Success, pre-registered, is a permutation p-value below 0.01 against the random ensemble and at least 20 of the 35 biological models showing strictly more memory kinds than their matched random networks. Publish seeds and the model identifiers." ;

    delphi:proposedTest "Permutation p below 0.01 and strict enrichment in at least 20 of 35 models. Otherwise memory in this protocol is not enriched relative to the matched random networks." ;
    delphi:context "Fails if: The random networks meet or exceed the biological memory rate. That refutes the biological-signature reading for this match. A probe implementation that cannot reproduce the paper's count on the original 35 models invalidates the run before the null is interpreted." ;
    delphi:hypothesisType "approach/computation" ;
    skos:note "Steps: 1. Pin the 35 BioModels identifiers from the paper before simulating. 2. Build at least 10 matched random networks for each, signs randomized. 3. Run the five probes with the paper's protocol. 4. Compute the paired permutation test. 5. Require p below 0.01 and at least 20 of 35 models strictly enriched." ;
    skos:note "Difficulty (proposer's estimate of completion within about a month of agent time): hard" ;
    skos:note "Tool: ode-simulation" ;
    skos:note "Tool: biomodels" ;
    skos:note "Tool: random-network-nulls" ;
    skos:note "Tool: data-test" ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2022-grn-learning-01> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2022-grn-learning-08> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2022-grn-learning-11> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2022-grn-learning-14> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2022-grn-learning-16> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biomodels/> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.isci.2021.102131> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi/blob/ee98025a1960b300fcc06aa2106f51118b60f565/problems/approaches/grok-4-7.json> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/grn-memory-generic-or-biological> a delphi:Concept, schema:Question ;
    rdfs:label "Is memory in gene regulatory network models generic or a biological signature?" .

  <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/biomodels/> dct:title "BioModels" ;
    dct:description "The pathway models named by Biswas et al. 2021." .
  <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.isci.2021.102131> dct:title "Gene regulatory networks exhibit several kinds of memory: Quantification of memory in biological and random transcriptional networks" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Biswas, Manicka, Hoel and Levin 2021, Gene regulatory networks exhibit several kinds of memory" .
}

